// =====================================================================================================================================
// File          : StaffSteps.java
// Package       : stepdefinitions.BISS.STAFF
// Purpose       : Single consolidated step definition library for every BISS internal (staff) portal feature:
//                 MAPS, SIM, CORRESPONDENCE, PAYMENTS, SCHEME, ACTIVE FARMER, AMS and OPENSHIFT.
//                 Features: src/test/resources/Test_Cases/BISS/STAFF/...
//
// Common Background : All staff features log in through the internal portal (CENTEST or OpenShift), open the
//                     BISS application, and then work from the Home screen or a named tab. The login and
//                     application-open steps are shared by every feature in this library.
//
// DB Data       : Herds, parcels and reference numbers come from the Oracle DB through utilities.StaffTestData.
//                 Feature files never name a row index - they ask for "the next submitted herd" and this class
//                 takes the next unused value of the relevant pool. That keeps sections independent and the
//                 features free of Excel-era row references.
//
// Notes         : - Declarative step wording. A single business step (e.g. "requests a map with the following
//                   settings") performs the whole UI interaction sequence internally, so the feature files
//                   describe intent and this class owns the mechanics.
//                 - Staff usernames stay hardcoded in the features: they are permission fixtures, not test
//                   data. Each carries a specific role the scenario depends on.
//                 - Passwords resolve from TestData.xlsx via the "TD:Password" mechanism.
//
// PLAYWRIGHT MIGRATION (05-10-2026) - same step texts, same Object Repository keys, same click order:
//   Selenium                                                     Playwright
//   Hooks.STAFF_* lists filled by the @staffdata hook        ->  StaffTestData.pool(kind, schemeYear), loaded the first
//                                                                time a step asks (see StaffTestData for tags and sizes)
//   getDriver().findElements(By).isEmpty()/isDisplayed()     ->  UiHelpers.isVisible(locator, seconds) - first match,
//                                                                never throws
//   findElement(By).getText() / getAttribute("textContent")  ->  Locator.innerText() / Locator.textContent()
//   getDriver().navigate().to(Hooks.iUrl)                    ->  UiHelpers.navigateTo(staff login address, see below)
//   switchTo().activeElement().sendKeys(Keys.TAB)            ->  UiHelpers.pressKey("Tab")
//   Thread.sleep(ms)                                         ->  pause(ms) (page.waitForTimeout - same duration)
//   WebDriverWait numberOfWindowsToBe + window handles       ->  BrowserContext.waitForPage + Page.close
//   iAction("CHECKBOX", ..., null)                           ->  Playwright CHECKBOX needs CHECK / UNCHECK, so:
//                                                                  toggles (SIM indicator, Force Majeure) -> CLICK
//                                                                  Eh change request (must end ticked)    -> CHECK
//
// Other changes (each marked "Change from Selenium" at the place it happens):
//   - The login steps open the staff login page when it is not already on screen: staff.url, or a StaffURL column
//     in the Config sheet, otherwise Hooks.iUrl as in Selenium.
//   - Map generation polling (500 x 5 s in Selenium) reads staff.map.poll.attempts / staff.map.poll.seconds,
//     with the same defaults. A missing first row is logged and polled again instead of failing at once.
//   - Absence checks ("should not have access", "no late penalty") look for PROBE_SECONDS before deciding the
//     element is absent, instead of a single immediate findElements.
//   - The [STEP] log lines show the values used instead of the {string} placeholders.
//
// Updated 15-10-2026 (SIM pack, TC_07 / 08 / 09 rewritten in this vocabulary):
//   - "the staff user opens the {string} screen" (side menu), "changes the SIM opt-in and submits with note",
//     "the SIM tick state should be readable ..." / "... should have changed" (TC_08 reads the tick before the change)
//   - SSO Administration: login into the SSO app, "replaces the BISS roles of user ... with the following" (one step
//     for the legacy 15-step role reset), "signs out of the portal"
//   - Payments: "the supplementary payment request form should be available"
//   - "should not have access to the {string} tab" now checks the named tab (it always looked for Map Printing)
//   - SIM / history Object Repository keys replaced by the XPaths the Selenium framework ran with
//   - History: the newest row must be dated today; "the latest history entry should mention {string}"
//
// Updated 15-10-2026 (Scheme Selection / Query Letter / AMS / Active Farmer pack, TC_12 / 14 / 15 / 18):
//   - Scheme selection: "notes the selection state of the following schemes", "... should have the opposite
//     selection", "... should have their noted selection", "the scheme selection screen should be displayed";
//     the selection state is read from the scheme-selected / scheme-not-selected class; the details dialogs take
//     scheme | title; the card checks by position read the title and the full name at that position
//   - "the application history should record {string} today"
//   - Query letter: Correspondence header tab; the preview passes on a new tab or an in-page preview
//   - AMS: client details, partner herd tabs, column headers, pagination, status icon hover
//   - "the Active Farmer screen should be displayed"
//   - Scheme / AMS / query letter / Active Farmer Object Repository keys replaced by the Selenium XPaths
//
// Updated 16-10-2026 (BISS Letters / Active Farmer notes / OpenShift / Home screen / CISYF payments pack, TC_06 / 13 / 16 /
//                     17 / 20):
//   - Payments: "opens the Payments screen for the next payment herd" / "... for the same herd", the BISS / CRISS / CISYF
//     columns, Total DPS Payment = sum of the net payment amounts, Reduction Type columns and rows
//   - Active Farmer: the result is a radio button, the notes box is in biss-active-farmer-admin-notes, the appeal upload
//     uses Test_Data/Cover_Letter.pdf, "the start admin check confirmation should be offered" (no stop applied)
//   - Coordination amendment: Save fails on a form error and logs the confirmation message
//   - Farmer search uses the Search By radio button
//
